{"title":"Career Roadmap · Cath-Lab Technologist","role":"Cath-Lab Technologist","summary":"A Cath-Lab Technologist is an allied-health professional who supports cardiologists and the interventional team during cardiac catheterization and minimally invasive cardiovascular procedures. The role combines patient preparation, sterile technique, imaging-system operation, procedure-room readiness, hemodynamic monitoring, device preparation, documentation, and emergency support.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Cardiac Care / Cardiovascular Technology"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Cath-Lab Technologist is an allied-health professional who supports cardiologists and the interventional team during cardiac catheterization and minimally invasive cardiovascular procedures. The role combines patient preparation, sterile technique, imaging-system operation, procedure-room readiness, hemodynamic monitoring, device preparation, documentation, and emergency support."},{"type":"p","text":"Common procedure exposure may include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Coronary angiography"},{"text":"Percutaneous coronary intervention (PCI)"},{"text":"Balloon angioplasty"},{"text":"Stent procedures"},{"text":"Temporary pacing procedures"},{"text":"Structural-heart interventions"},{"text":"Peripheral vascular procedures"},{"text":"Electrophysiology procedures, depending on the centre"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The technologist works as part of a multidisciplinary team that may include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Interventional cardiologists"},{"text":"Cardiologists"},{"text":"Nurses"},{"text":"Anaesthesia professionals"},{"text":"Radiographers/imaging personnel"},{"text":"Perfusion and other cardiovascular specialists"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Professional note","text":"The exact scope of practice varies by hospital and applicable professional requirements. Invasive clinical decisions and procedures remain under the responsibility of appropriately qualified clinicians."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Career Stage","Typical Development"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Anatomy, physiology, cardiovascular foundation"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Cardiac technology + cath-lab fundamentals"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Interventional procedures + hemodynamic monitoring"}],[{"text":"Clinical training"},{"text":"Supervised cath-lab experience"}],[{"text":"0–2 years"},{"text":"Cath-Lab Technologist / Cardiovascular Technologist"}],[{"text":"2–5 years"},{"text":"Experienced Cath-Lab Technologist"}],[{"text":"5–8 years"},{"text":"Senior / Lead Technologist"}],[{"text":"8–12 years"},{"text":"Cath-Lab Supervisor / Coordinator"}],[{"text":"12+ years"},{"text":"Cardiovascular Services / Cath-Lab Operations Management"}]]}]},{"heading":"Year 1 — Biomedical & Cardiovascular Foundation","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Core subjects"},{"type":"p","text":"Build strong knowledge of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human anatomy"},{"text":"Physiology"},{"text":"Biochemistry"},{"text":"Microbiology"},{"text":"Pathology"},{"text":"Pharmacology fundamentals"},{"text":"Medical terminology"},{"text":"Patient care"},{"text":"Infection control"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Cardiovascular sciences"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Heart anatomy"},{"text":"Cardiac chambers"},{"text":"Valves"},{"text":"Coronary arteries"},{"text":"Cardiac conduction system"},{"text":"Cardiac cycle"},{"text":"Blood pressure"},{"text":"Cardiac output"},{"text":"Peripheral circulation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"ECG foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"ECG leads"},{"text":"P waves"},{"text":"QRS complex"},{"text":"T waves"},{"text":"Heart rate"},{"text":"Rhythm basics"},{"text":"Common abnormalities"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 objective"},{"type":"p","text":"Build strong cardiovascular anatomy, physiology and patient-care fundamentals before entering invasive cardiac technology."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Cardiac & Cath-Lab Technology"},{"type":"h","text":"Cath-lab fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Catheterization laboratory layout"},{"text":"Fluoroscopy"},{"text":"Digital imaging"},{"text":"C-arm systems"},{"text":"Contrast injection"},{"text":"Radiation protection"},{"text":"Sterile field"},{"text":"Catheter and guidewire systems"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Equipment"},{"type":"p","text":"Become familiar with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Angiography system"},{"text":"Fluoroscopy system"},{"text":"Hemodynamic monitoring system"},{"text":"Contrast injector"},{"text":"ECG monitor"},{"text":"Defibrillator"},{"text":"Temporary pacing equipment"},{"text":"Intra-aortic balloon pump awareness"},{"text":"Emergency trolley"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Cardiovascular procedures"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop theoretical knowledge of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Diagnostic coronary angiography"},{"text":"PCI"},{"text":"Balloon angioplasty"},{"text":"Stent deployment"},{"text":"Peripheral angiography"},{"text":"Temporary pacing"},{"text":"Right/left heart catheterization"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Advanced Cath-Lab Practice"},{"type":"h","text":"Patient preparation"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn the workflow:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Patient Identification","Clinical History","Consent Verification","Allergy / Contrast Screening","Baseline Vitals & ECG","IV / Access Preparation","Sterile Preparation","Procedure","Hemodynamic Monitoring","Post-Procedure Recovery"]},{"type":"h","text":"Hemodynamic monitoring"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Arterial pressure"},{"text":"Venous pressure"},{"text":"Heart rate"},{"text":"ECG"},{"text":"Oxygen saturation"},{"text":"Cardiac output concepts"},{"text":"Pressure waveforms"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Develop familiarity with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Aortic pressure"},{"text":"Right atrial pressure"},{"text":"Right ventricular pressure"},{"text":"Pulmonary artery pressure"},{"text":"Pulmonary capillary wedge pressure"}]}]},{"heading":"Cath-Lab Procedure Support","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The technologist may support different stages of the procedure according to institutional scope."},{"type":"h","text":"Before procedure"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Prepare the room"},{"text":"Check equipment"},{"text":"Prepare sterile supplies"},{"text":"Verify required catheters and devices"},{"text":"Check imaging system"},{"text":"Prepare contrast equipment"},{"text":"Ensure emergency equipment is available"}]},{"type":"h","text":"During procedure"},{"type":"p","text":"Support the team with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Equipment handling"},{"text":"Imaging workflow"},{"text":"Hemodynamic monitoring"},{"text":"Device preparation"},{"text":"Contrast workflow"},{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Radiation-safety procedures"}]},{"type":"h","text":"After procedure"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Equipment cleanup"},{"text":"Disposal of consumables"},{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Patient transfer support"},{"text":"Restocking"},{"text":"Equipment readiness"}]}]},{"heading":"Cardiovascular Devices","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop familiarity with:"},{"type":"h","text":"Diagnostic equipment"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Diagnostic catheters"},{"text":"Guidewires"},{"text":"Sheaths"},{"text":"Pressure-monitoring systems"}]},{"type":"h","text":"PCI equipment"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Guiding catheters"},{"text":"Guidewires"},{"text":"Balloons"},{"text":"Coronary stents"},{"text":"Aspiration devices"},{"text":"Drug-delivery systems"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Other devices"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Temporary pacing wires"},{"text":"Closure devices"},{"text":"Intravascular imaging systems"},{"text":"Atherectomy systems"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The student should understand indications and equipment handling, while actual device selection and deployment remain under the responsible clinical team."}]},{"heading":"Imaging & Radiation Safety","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Cath labs use ionizing radiation, making radiation safety essential."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"ALARA principle"},{"text":"Radiation exposure"},{"text":"Scatter radiation"},{"text":"Distance"},{"text":"Shielding"},{"text":"Protective barriers"},{"text":"Lead aprons"},{"text":"Thyroid protection"},{"text":"Radiation monitoring"},{"text":"Dose documentation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Radiation-safety principle"},{"type":"p","text":"Minimize Time"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Maximize Distance"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"flow","items":["Use Appropriate Shielding","Reduce Occupational Exposure"]},{"type":"p","text":"Develop familiarity with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Dose-area product"},{"text":"Fluoroscopy time"},{"text":"Cumulative dose"},{"text":"Radiation warning systems"}]}]},{"heading":"Sterile Technique & Infection Control","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Cath-lab procedures require strict infection-control discipline."},{"type":"p","text":"Master:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Hand hygiene"},{"text":"Surgical scrub"},{"text":"PPE"},{"text":"Sterile gowning"},{"text":"Sterile gloving"},{"text":"Sterile-field maintenance"},{"text":"Skin preparation"},{"text":"Catheter handling"},{"text":"Sharps safety"},{"text":"Biomedical waste management"},{"text":"Environmental cleaning"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the importance of maintaining sterility around:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Vascular access"},{"text":"Catheters"},{"text":"Guidewires"},{"text":"Devices"},{"text":"Procedure trays"}]}]},{"heading":"Emergency Preparedness","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Cath-lab procedures can deteriorate rapidly, so the technologist must be prepared for emergencies."},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the workflow for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cardiac arrest"},{"text":"Arrhythmias"},{"text":"Acute coronary complications"},{"text":"Hypotension"},{"text":"Hypertension"},{"text":"Contrast reactions"},{"text":"Bleeding"},{"text":"Vascular complications"},{"text":"Perforation"},{"text":"Stroke"},{"text":"Air embolism"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Emergency workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["Recognize Deterioration","Alert Clinical Team","Monitoring","Emergency Equipment","Resuscitation Support","Defibrillation / Pacing Support","Documentation"]},{"type":"p","text":"BLS/CPR training is highly valuable."}]},{"heading":"Contrast-Media Knowledge","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Contrast media purpose"},{"text":"Contrast administration workflow"},{"text":"Allergy history"},{"text":"Renal-risk considerations"},{"text":"Contrast reactions"},{"text":"Extravasation"},{"text":"Emergency response"},{"text":"Documentation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The technologist should follow institutional protocols and work within the authorized scope for contrast preparation and administration."}]},{"heading":"Projects to Build","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — Cath-Lab Equipment Checklist"},{"type":"p","text":"Create a checklist covering:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Imaging system"},{"text":"Hemodynamic monitor"},{"text":"Contrast injector"},{"text":"ECG"},{"text":"Defibrillator"},{"text":"Pacing equipment"},{"text":"Emergency trolley"},{"text":"Sterile supplies"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2 — Coronary Angiography Workflow"},{"type":"p","text":"Document:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Patient Preparation","Vascular Access","Catheter Navigation","Coronary Imaging","Hemodynamic Monitoring","Intervention if Required","Post-Procedure Care"]},{"type":"p","text":"Use academic/simulated information rather than identifiable patient records."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 3 — Radiation-Safety Audit"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Fluoroscopy time"},{"text":"Staff positioning"},{"text":"Shield usage"},{"text":"Dose monitoring"},{"text":"Radiation-protection compliance"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 4 — Cath-Lab Emergency Preparedness"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop a simulated emergency checklist for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cardiac arrest"},{"text":"Contrast reaction"},{"text":"Acute arrhythmia"},{"text":"Hypotension"},{"text":"Major bleeding"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 5 — Hemodynamic Waveform Portfolio"},{"type":"p","text":"Create a learning portfolio covering:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Aortic pressure"},{"text":"Right atrial pressure"},{"text":"Right ventricular pressure"},{"text":"Pulmonary artery pressure"},{"text":"Wedge pressure"}]}]},{"heading":"Skill Matrix","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Skill","Importance"],"rows":[[{"text":"Cardiovascular Anatomy"},{"text":"★★★★★"}],[{"text":"Cardiac Physiology"},{"text":"★★★★★"}],[{"text":"Cath-Lab Workflow"},{"text":"★★★★★"}],[{"text":"Sterile Technique"},{"text":"★★★★★"}],[{"text":"Radiation Safety"},{"text":"★★★★★"}],[{"text":"Hemodynamic Monitoring"},{"text":"★★★★★"}],[{"text":"Cardiovascular Equipment"},{"text":"★★★★★"}],[{"text":"Emergency Response"},{"text":"★★★★★"}],[{"text":"ECG"},{"text":"★★★★☆"}],[{"text":"Contrast Safety"},{"text":"★★★★☆"}],[{"text":"Catheter/Guidewire Knowledge"},{"text":"★★★★☆"}],[{"text":"Patient Preparation"},{"text":"★★★★★"}],[{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"★★★★☆"}],[{"text":"Infection Control"},{"text":"★★★★★"}],[{"text":"Communication"},{"text":"★★★★☆"}]]}]},{"heading":"Equipment & Technical Skills","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Gain familiarity with:"},{"type":"h","text":"Imaging"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Fluoroscopy"},{"text"